---

<section id="faq" class="section faq-section">
  <div class="site-shell faq-section__inner">
    <div class="faq-section__intro">
      <h2>FAQ</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details>
        <summary>I'm not naturally tidy. Will this even work for me?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>Yes. I design for your real habits, not a perfect lifestyle.</p>

<p>I don't expect you to become a different person or suddenly enjoy cleaning. Instead, we look at where things naturally land, create better drop zones, and make it easier to put things away without thinking about it.</p>

<p>The goal isn't perfection. It's a home that's easier to live in on both your productive days and your low-energy ones.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Why is this less expensive than traditional interior design?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>Because it's designed for a different kind of problem.</p>

          <p>Traditional interior design is often the right choice when you're renovating, buying custom furniture, or redesigning a home from scratch.</p>

          <p>Most renters don't need that.</p>

          <p>They need help making the space they already have work better.</p>

          <p>That's what this service is for: improving layout, flow, storage, and everyday functionality without the cost, disruption, or commitment of a full interior design project.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Will you tell me to get rid of lots of things?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>We'll gently edit, but I'm not here to police your belongings. My focus is to make what you keep <strong>work harder</strong>: easier to find, easier to put away, and less visually overwhelming.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Do you do renovations or anything permanent?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>No. Everything we do is 100% renter-friendly and completely reversible. No walls down, no built-ins, no drilling that will upset your landlord. We work with layout, movable furniture, lighting and storage you can take with you.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Do you only work in person? What if I'm moving soon?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>For Hong Kong rentals, I recommend in-person sessions because moving things physically is a big part of the process. If you're moving and don't have access yet, we can do Session 1 online using your floor plan and photos, then do Session 2 in person after you move in.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Why bother, if it's just a rental?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>Because a one-year lease is still 365 days of your actual life.</p>
          <p>You wake up there, come home tired there, relax there, and spend time with the people and hobbies you care about there.</p>
          <p>And if you're already paying Hong Kong rent every month, it makes sense to have a home that actually supports your day-to-day life.</p>
          <p><strong>You don't have to wait until you own a property to enjoy living in it.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>I live with a partner / roommates. Can we still do this?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>Yes. There will always be one main client and point of contact, but I'm happy to work in homes with more than one person. If we're working on <strong>shared spaces</strong> (like the living room), I ask that everyone who uses them is aware of the project and joins at least part of Session 1 so we can make decisions that feel fair and realistic for everyone. If we're only working on <strong>your private room</strong>, I'll stay within that space.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
  <center><h3>You're already paying to live there. You deserve to enjoy coming home to it.</h3></center>

<style>
  .faq-section {
    background: var(--section-bg, var(--bg));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--section-border, rgba(199, 148, 92, 0.2));
    padding: 2.5rem 0 3rem;
  }

  .faq-section__intro h2 {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .faq-list {
    max-width: 60%;
    margin: 1.5rem auto 0;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--section-accent, var(--accent-tan));
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .faq-list {
      max-width: 100%;
      margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
      border-left: none;
      padding-left: 0;
    }
  }

  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--section-heading, var(--heading));
    list-style: none;
  }
  summary::marker { color: var(--section-accent, var(--accent-teal)); }
  summary::after {
    content: "+";
    float: right;
    color: var(--section-accent, var(--accent-teal));
  }
  details[open] summary { color: var(--section-accent, var(--accent-teal)); }
  details[open] summary::after { content: "–"; }
  details p { margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--section-text, var(--text)); }
</style>

<script>
  // FAQ Accordion - only one open at a time
  const faqDetails = document.querySelectorAll('#faq details');
  
  faqDetails.forEach(detail => {
    detail.addEventListener('toggle', (e) => {
      if (detail.open) {
        // Close all other open details (accordion behavior)
        faqDetails.forEach(otherDetail => {
          if (otherDetail !== detail && otherDetail.open) {
            otherDetail.open = false;
          }
        });
      }
    });
  });
</script>
